PART 4: THE CYCLE CAVEAT — freeness FAILS for Hamiltonian CYCLES
======================================================================
  C3 cyclic triangle (0->1->2->0):
    |Aut| = 3, #HamCycles (arc sets) = 1
    |Aut| divides #HC ? False  (1 % 3 = 1)
    (non-identity sigma, fixed cycle) incidences: 2  -> action NOT FREE
    orbit sizes: [1]  (free would force all = 3)
  RQ5 circulant (i -> i+1, i+2 mod 5):
    |Aut| = 5, #HamCycles (arc sets) = 2
    |Aut| divides #HC ? False  (2 % 5 = 2)
    (non-identity sigma, fixed cycle) incidences: 8  -> action NOT FREE
    orbit sizes: [1, 1]  (free would force all = 5)
  CONTRAST (paths on RQ5): |Aut|=5, H=15, orbits=3, all of size |Aut|: True

